 roleInSystem:"Turns molecules into brands: companies in-license or make formulations, build them into doctor-recognised brands through large medical-representative (MR) field forces, and sell through ~65,000 stockists to India's chemists. In India almost every off-patent medicine is a 'branded generic', so brand and prescriber loyalty, not patents, decide market share.",
 whyItMatters:"This is the steadiest and highest-return profit pool in Indian pharma: no US-style price erosion, high gross margins (60-80%), modest capex and cash-rich balance sheets. It is also where the sector's best compounders (Sun's India business, Torrent, Abbott India, Mankind) live, and why consolidation deals in this layer command 30x+ EBITDA.",
 valuePoolDescription:"Pharmarack puts the IPM at ~₹2.4L Cr for calendar 2025 (+8.1%), with August 2026 value growth of 10.7%. Growth is mostly price and new launches (annual WPI-linked hikes on NLEM drugs, freer pricing on non-scheduled brands); volume growth is near zero. Chronic therapies (cardiac, anti-diabetic, CNS, GI) grow faster and are stickier than acute ones (anti-infectives, respiratory), so chronic-heavy portfolios earn premium valuations.",
